        <div class="introduction intro-story">
          <p class="reveal-text">I entered university in 2023, about a year after the debut of ChatGPT—a time when artificial intelligence was flourishing globally. Today, AI-powered coding agents are capable of handling the vast majority of tasks traditionally performed by programmers, whether in front-end development, back-end development, or software testing.</p>
          <p class="reveal-text">However, I believe it is a mistake to liken programmers to textile workers; after all, the spinning jenny could not think. At least for the near future, those who work with code will have more time and broader scope to explore areas like user experience, product design, and the intricacies of business logic—ultimately enabling them to create even better, more impactful work.</p>
